WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.459 --> 00:00:12.739
rushed into the farmyard.

2
00:00:12.759 --> 00:00:15.620
"I'm back!"

3
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.701
"Yay!" Izzie hugged Nina.

4
00:00:20.721 --> 00:00:23.082
"I missed you."

5
00:00:23.102 --> 00:00:26.203
"How was your trip to Korea?"

6
00:00:26.643 --> 00:00:27.463
Jason asked.

7
00:00:27.483 --> 00:00:30.184
"Fun!" Nina said.

8
00:00:31.744 --> 00:00:35.386
"My cousin Peter took me to beautiful royal palaces.

9
00:00:36.787 --> 00:00:40.969
We went to Namsan Tower and walked along Cheonggyecheon Stream.

10
00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.472
And I ate so many delicious foods."

11
00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:50.154
The kids went inside.

12
00:00:50.174 --> 00:00:56.758
"Speaking of food Bobby pointed to the recipe screen.

13
00:00:57.739 --> 00:00:59.980
"What are bulgogi cheesesteaks?"

14
00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:04.689
"Nina suggested this recipe," Chef said.

15
00:01:04.709 --> 00:01:10.610
"Peter and I ate beef bulgogi in Korea," Nina said.

16
00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:14.531
"It reminded me of Philly cheesesteaks from home.

17
00:01:15.952 --> 00:01:19.853
So Mom and I made a cheesesteak with bulgogi for him."

18
00:01:21.513 --> 00:01:22.834
Bobby patted his stomach.

19
00:01:22.854 --> 00:01:26.415
"Yum! Cheesesteak!"

20
00:01:26.435 --> 00:01:30.856
"First we'll marinate the beef," Chef said.

21
00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:32.721
"Later we'll cook it."

22
00:01:36.243 --> 00:01:37.924
Chef got some meat from the freezer.

23
00:01:37.944 --> 00:01:41.826
"I froze this for thirty minutes.

24
00:01:42.967 --> 00:01:45.208
It will be easier to slice into thin strips."

25
00:01:47.629 --> 00:01:48.910
He began slicing the meat.

26
00:01:51.932 --> 00:01:53.693
The kids started making the marinade.

27
00:01:55.354 --> 00:01:58.476
Nina chopped garlic, and Bobby and Izzie chopped green onions.

28
00:02:02.432 --> 00:02:05.875
Jason mixed together soy sauce, sesame oil, and brown sugar.

29
00:02:07.356 --> 00:02:09.638
Nina added grated pear and black pepper.

30
00:02:15.823 --> 00:02:19.346
put the meat and marinade in this container," Chef said.

31
00:02:25.591 --> 00:02:27.913
Jason stirred the mixture to coat the meat well.

32
00:02:29.255 --> 00:02:30.696
Then he sealed the container.

33
00:02:31.848 --> 00:02:34.390
"Now it goes into the refrigerator for two hours."

34
00:02:41.654 --> 00:02:42.615
"What's next?"

35
00:02:43.075 --> 00:02:43.816
Izzie asked.

36
00:02:43.836 --> 00:02:48.079
"Can I show everyone my photos from Korea?"

37
00:02:49.239 --> 00:02:50.480
Nina held up her phone.

38
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.542
"Sure," Chef said.

39
00:02:53.562 --> 00:02:56.224
"After that, we'll weed the garden."

40
00:03:01.964 --> 00:03:03.705
"Time to make the cheesesteaks!"

41
00:03:03.765 --> 00:03:04.386
Chef said.

42
00:03:04.406 --> 00:03:08.588
"Finally!" Bobby cheered.

43
00:03:10.549 --> 00:03:13.371
Inside, Chef got out two onions.

44
00:03:13.391 --> 00:03:15.512
"Let's slice these first.

45
00:03:16.513 --> 00:03:17.733
We need thin strips."

46
00:03:19.735 --> 00:03:21.216
"Wah!" Bobby said.

47
00:03:21.236 --> 00:03:23.797
"I'll try not to cry!"

48
00:03:26.519 --> 00:03:28.360
Everyone laughed and began slicing.

49
00:03:32.272 --> 00:03:35.453
Next Nina put two tablespoons of butter in a pan.

50
00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.214
Izzie added the olive oil.

51
00:03:39.475 --> 00:03:42.015
After the butter melted, Chef put in the onions.

52
00:03:45.297 --> 00:03:48.038
The onions turned soft and golden as Chef cooked them.

53
00:03:48.058 --> 00:03:51.579
"Bobby, please get a plate.

54
00:03:52.639 --> 00:03:54.820
We're going to remove the onions from the pan.

55
00:04:00.292 --> 00:04:02.654
Now we'll cook the meat over high heat."

56
00:04:04.616 --> 00:04:07.379
The meat sizzled as Chef dropped it into the hot pan.

57
00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:10.842
Bobby stirred the meat to cook it evenly.

58
00:04:13.144 --> 00:04:16.427
"Now we cut the sandwich rolls," Nina said.

59
00:04:18.188 --> 00:04:20.610
She sliced a long roll in half lengthwise.

60
00:04:20.630 --> 00:04:24.113
"Don't cut the roll all the way through.

61
00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:26.696
It should open like a book."

62
00:04:28.608 --> 00:04:30.410
Everyone carefully sliced their rolls.

63
00:04:32.511 --> 00:04:34.233
Chef topped the meat with the onions.

64
00:04:34.253 --> 00:04:36.595
"What's next, Nina?"

65
00:04:38.176 --> 00:04:40.638
"We add cheese and let it melt.

66
00:04:45.342 --> 00:04:48.865
Then we put the meat mixture on the rolls!"

67
00:04:50.346 --> 00:04:52.068
At last the cheesesteaks were ready.

68
00:04:56.311 --> 00:04:57.012
Bobby said.

69
00:04:58.616 --> 00:04:59.516
Nina smiled.

70
00:05:00.717 --> 00:05:02.457
But suddenly she felt sad.

71
00:05:04.038 --> 00:05:05.118
Her chin trembled.

72
00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:08.979
"Nina! What's wrong?"

73
00:05:09.439 --> 00:05:10.160
Izzie asked.

74
00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.241
"I miss Peter.

75
00:05:13.261 --> 00:05:17.182
I wish Seoul wasn't so far away."

76
00:05:17.202 --> 00:05:22.384
"Let's send him a photo of us eating bulgogi cheesesteaks!"

77
00:05:22.804 --> 00:05:23.624
Jason said.

78
00:05:25.972 --> 00:05:28.573
Nina took out her phone and burst out laughing.

79
00:05:28.593 --> 00:05:33.615
"I just got a text from Peter.

80
00:05:33.635 --> 00:05:36.197
Look at the photo he sent!"

81
00:05:38.418 --> 00:05:41.079
Nina's cousin was eating a bulgogi cheesesteak!

82
00:05:41.099 --> 00:05:45.721
"That's a wonderful thing about food," Chef said.

83
00:05:45.741 --> 00:05:49.723
"It brings us together—even when we're far apart."

84
00:05:51.783 --> 00:05:52.724
Nina nodded.

85
00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:55.886
"That makes me so happy!"
